        "body": "Write the girls by their initials. Start: F G H I J. Finish: I G F J H.\n\n- For I to finish first she must pass F, G and H: at least 3 overtakes.\n- G finishes ahead of F, but G started behind F, so G must overtake F: 1 more.\n- J finishes ahead of H, but J started behind H, so J must overtake H: 1 more.\n\nThese are five different pairs whose order changes, and each change needs at least one overtake, so at least $5$ points. All other pairs keep their order.\n\nIt can be done with exactly 5 overtakes, one at a time: FGHIJ, FGIHJ, FIGHJ, IFGHJ, IGFHJ, IGFJH.\n\n**Answer: (E) 5**"
      }
