        "title": "Count how often each $2\\times2$ square was chosen",
        "body": "Let $P,Q,R,S$ be the numbers of times the top-left, top-right, bottom-right and bottom-left $2\\times2$ squares were picked. Each corner cell of the grid lies in exactly one of these squares, so the bottom-left corner shows $S=13$ and the cell marked $?$ shows $R$.\n\nThe top-middle cell lies in the top-left and top-right squares, so $P+Q=18$. The centre cell lies in all four squares, so $47=P+Q+R+S=18+R+13$, giving $R=16$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 16**"
